From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 11:25:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 12/15] regex: share literal bytecode and specialize bounded
 operations

Borrow immutable compiled literal bytecode while creating fresh RegExp
objects with independent lastIndex and named-group initialization. Honor
overridden exec methods, and avoid discarded match arrays for eligible
Boolean tests while retaining captures and legacy match state.

Generate bounded AOT matchers for supported literals and repetitions,
including UTF-16 non-Unicode case equivalents and capture-free forward
alternatives. Validate branch targets, bound pending alternatives and
suffix retries, and preserve interpreter fallback and work budgets.
Index Unicode canonicalization tables by immutable page directories.

Lower guarded whole operations on fresh unescaped regex literals:
indexed tests, empty replacement, unchanged lowercase replacement and
replacement equality. Preserve lookup/evaluation order, coercion,
UTF-16 indexing, rooting and original IR on a declined fast path.

Bound generated descriptor and matcher storage per module. Keep normal
and split-C emission, interpreter parity, custom execution, captures,
alternatives and exhaustive supported-codepoint coverage with the
engine/compiler integration. This does not replace the general matcher.
